WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.659 --> 00:00:05.029
Add some of Avengers: Endgame's crew to the
list of people who weren't thrilled with Thor's

00:00:05.029 --> 00:00:06.080
husky new look.

00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:10.340
In a recent interview with Empire magazine,
the flick's screenwriters Christopher Markus

00:00:10.349 --> 00:00:14.730
and Stephen McFeely revealed that the Thunder
God's new appearance didn't sit so well with

00:00:14.730 --> 00:00:16.740
some of those who were on the production's
set.

00:00:16.940 --> 00:00:20.830
In case you're one of the six people who hasn't
seen the film yet, be advised that spoilers

00:00:20.830 --> 00:00:22.760
for Avengers: Endgame follow.

00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:27.519
You'll recall that after Endgame's five-year
time jump, Professor Hulk and Rocket set out

00:00:27.519 --> 00:00:32.130
for New Asgard to track down Thor, who had
dealt with his failure to prevent the Decimation

00:00:32.130 --> 00:00:34.400
in a rather unhealthy manner.

00:00:34.720 --> 00:00:37.740
"You should've gone for the head."

00:00:41.080 --> 00:00:46.020
Specifically, he had spent the previous half-decade
drinking enough beer to drown an elephant,

00:00:46.020 --> 00:00:50.480
playing Fortnite, and growing the type of
gut you rarely see on superheroes.

00:00:50.520 --> 00:00:54.440
Many fans felt that Thor's obvious depression
and new, portly physique were being played

00:00:54.440 --> 00:00:59.090
for laughs, although later scenes treated
his fragile mental state with sensitivity,

00:00:59.090 --> 00:01:03.250
allowing it to play into his larger character
arc and making the near-immortal god that

00:01:03.250 --> 00:01:05.220
much more relatable for the audience.

00:01:05.220 --> 00:01:09.280
According to Markus and McFeely, a few unnamed
crew members took issue.

00:01:09.460 --> 00:01:10.600
Markus told Empire,

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:15.100
"There was a sad moment where it was like,
'We've got this gross, disgusting body for

00:01:15.100 --> 00:01:15.600
Thor now.'

00:01:15.700 --> 00:01:19.660
And then they unveiled it and it's just kind
of like everybody else's body here."

00:01:20.740 --> 00:01:21.800
"That's a nice way of putting it."

00:01:22.360 --> 00:01:23.360
McFeely added,

00:01:23.560 --> 00:01:27.040
"There were many people on set who were angry
at us about doing that to Thor."

00:01:27.480 --> 00:01:31.680
McFeely, however, implied that the on-set
anger wasn't necessarily because they felt

00:01:31.690 --> 00:01:35.890
that Thor's condition was being handled with
a lack of tact, but because the screenwriters

00:01:35.890 --> 00:01:39.200
had seen fit to send the character on his
downward spiral at all.

00:01:39.350 --> 00:01:43.500
Markus agreed, saying that it was simply a
brutal shock to see just how despondent the

00:01:43.500 --> 00:01:45.020
mighty Odinson had become.

00:01:45.840 --> 00:01:46.780
"I don't drink tea."

00:01:47.180 --> 00:01:48.060
"What do you drink?"

00:01:48.720 --> 00:01:49.580
"Not tea."

00:01:53.320 --> 00:01:57.540
Nobody, not even the God of Thunder, could
put away that much beer without packing on

00:01:57.550 --> 00:02:01.990
a few pounds in the process - and that it's
not like Thor went on any kind of crash diet

00:02:01.990 --> 00:02:06.360
before jumping back into the mix to take part
in the Avengers' most important mission yet.

00:02:06.480 --> 00:02:10.740
He would still test the structural integrity
of the Megingjord, if you catch our drift.

00:02:10.980 --> 00:02:15.050
"We just gotta load Tony's old hulkbuster armor, the prototype for Cap's new shield, and

00:02:16.060 --> 00:02:16.660
The Megin...

00:02:17.560 --> 00:02:18.160
The megin…

00:02:19.240 --> 00:02:20.300
Thor's magic belt."

00:02:20.800 --> 00:02:24.380
Markus defended the decision to keep Thor
beefy throughout Endgame, saying,

00:02:24.620 --> 00:02:27.080
"I like that heroes come in all shapes and
sizes.

00:02:27.260 --> 00:02:32.040
[Thor] comes from a tradition of guys like
Volstagg, of a big, ass-kicking fat guy.

00:02:32.040 --> 00:02:33.820
There's no reason that he has to slim down."

00:02:34.220 --> 00:02:38.480
We hope that the character of Thor continues
to be explored in interesting and unexpected

00:02:38.480 --> 00:02:43.090
ways, as he may be the only original Avenger
who will continue to be a presence in the

00:02:43.090 --> 00:02:44.000
films of Phase 4.

00:02:44.080 --> 00:02:48.400
Endgame's conclusion saw him heading off into
the cosmos to find new adventures with the

00:02:48.400 --> 00:02:53.440
Guardians of the Galaxy, and Tessa Thompson
- who portrays New Asgard's new ruler Valkyrie

00:02:53.440 --> 00:02:58.700
- recently let slip to the Los Angeles Times
that he might also very well be the first

00:02:58.700 --> 00:03:01.180
MCU character to get a fourth solo flick.

00:03:01.420 --> 00:03:04.920
Of course, it wouldn't be too surprising if
the God of Thunder were to shed all those

00:03:04.920 --> 00:03:09.350
extra pounds before his next appearance, but
one could simply chalk that up to there being

00:03:09.350 --> 00:03:11.380
no decent beer in space.

